I'm not sure if this was mentioned before (or even fixed) but it's possible
to #loot until you collapse under your load.  One would not of course pick
up more things than one can carry, not depending where one picks them from.

And to say this again, it should be possible to read and quaff objects which
you haven't picked up, just as it is possible to eat without picking up.

What about adding a new ailment: bad eyesight ?  Not as bad as blindness,
but you wouldn't be able to recognize monsters and objects when they aren't
close to you.  A maximum case would of course be blindness (what about having
white canes, which somehow aid in blindess) ?  And, when you have bad eyesight
it would take longer to figure out scrolls and spellbooks, and reading them
on the floor would become impossible.

I think the spellbook's usefullness is very limited, since you have to have
REALLY good Magical scores to be able to use the more advanced spellbooks at
all.  And even then, they can be faded already on the first reading !
